Ladybird answers screen.availWidth and availHeight from the available
screen rect the UI reports, which the Qt UI takes from QScreen::
availableGeometry(). Blink’s Screen::availWidth() reads ScreenInfo::
available_rect, the display’s work area; WebKit’s screenAvailableRect()
returns the NSScreen’s visibleFrame; Gecko’s nsScreen::GetAvailRect()
reads widget::Screen’s avail rect, which ScreenHelperCocoa.mm fills from
[NSScreen visibleFrame]. QScreen::availableGeometry() wraps that same
visibleFrame on macOS, so all four agree there.
